{"collection":{"version":"1.1","href":"http://images-api.nasa.gov/search?q=Gemini+pressure+suit&media_type=image&year_start=1964&year_end=1966&page_size=25","items":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S64-20199/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1964-07-29T00:00:00Z","description":"S64-20199 (10 Sept. 1964) --- View of the Gemini-4 prime crew and backup crew in pressure suits. They are standing around a model of the Gemini spacecraft. From left to right are astronauts Edward H. White II,  pilot; James A. McDivitt, command pilot; Frank Borman and James A. Lovell Jr., backup crew.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S64-20199","title":"Gemini 4 - Prime and Backup Crew"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S64-20199/S64-20199~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":231000,"height":1024},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S64-20199/S64-20199~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":70000,"height":512},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S64-20199/S64-20199~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":70000,"height":512},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S64-20199/S64-20199~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1919,"size":470000,"height":1535},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S64-20199/S64-20199~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-14457/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-02-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-14457 (23 Feb. 1965) --- Both members of the Gemini-Titan 3 prime crew egress through the left, or command pilot's, hatch into the Gulf of Mexico during specialized training in egress from the Gemini spacecraft. Astronaut Virgil I. Grissom, the command pilot, has already climbed into a raft, as astronaut John W. Young, pilot, egresses from the spacecraft.","keywords":["ASTRONAUT TRAINING","ASTRONAUTS","EGRESS","GEMINI FLIGHT 3","GEMINI PROJECT","GEMINI SPACECRAFT","PRESSURE SUITS","SPACE SUITS","WATER LANDING"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-14457","title":"Gemini 3 prime crew egress throught command pilot's hatch during training"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-14457/s65-14457~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1276,"size":203000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-14457/s65-14457~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":638,"size":55000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-14457/s65-14457~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":638,"size":55000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-14457/s65-14457~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1914,"size":450000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-14457/s65-14457~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-41955/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-07-12T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-41955 (12 July 1965) --- Astronaut Charles Conrad Jr. receives assistance with his pressure suit during suiting up and ingress test activity at Pad 16, Cape Kennedy, Florida in preparation for the Gemini-5 spaceflight.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-41955","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-V - TEST - CAPE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-41955/s65-41955~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":134000,"height":1008},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-41955/s65-41955~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":39000,"height":504},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-41955/s65-41955~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":39000,"height":504},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-41955/s65-41955~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":302000,"height":1513},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-41955/s65-41955~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-54319/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-09-22T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-54319 (22 Sept. 1965) --- Astronaut Walter M. Schirra Jr., command pilot of the Gemini-6 prime crew, undergoes weight and balance tests in the Pyrotechnic Installation Building, Merritt Island, Kennedy Space Center, Florida. Photo credit: NASA or National Aeronautics and Space Administration","keywords":["ASTRONAUTS","BALANCE","EJECTION SEATS","GEMINI 6 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","TESTS","PRESSURE SUITS","WEIGHT (MASS)"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-54319","title":"Astronaut Walter Schirra during weight and balance test"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-54319/s65-54319~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":139000,"height":1007},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-54319/s65-54319~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":46000,"height":503},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-54319/s65-54319~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":46000,"height":503},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-54319/s65-54319~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":289000,"height":1511},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-54319/s65-54319~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-27990/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-03-01T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-27990 (March 1966) --- Astronaut Eugene A. Cernan, pilot for the Gemini-9 spaceflight, works out procedures for his historic space excursion in a unique manned Aerospace Flight Simulator at LTV Corp. at Dallas, Texas. The LTV simulator is used frequently by NASA astronauts for a variety of space programs maneuvers to provide many of the sensations and visual scenes of actual spaceflight. Controlled through a complex of computers, the device makes it possible for the astronauts to work out procedures, solve problems and simulate missions in real time with great accuracy. The astronaut rides in a spacecraft-like gondola which moves in roll, pitch and yaw in response to his controls and accurate computer inputs. The simulator's usual spacecraft displays and canopy have been removed and AMU backpack complete with control electronics installed. The astronaut makes his simulated flight in an inflated pressure suit and with the NASA-developed Extravehicular Life Support system chest pack which will be used in the Gemini flight. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-27990","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-9- TRAINING - AEROSPACE FLIGHT SIMULATOR - PILOT - TX"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-27990/s66-27990~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":838,"size":138000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-27990/s66-27990~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":419,"size":41000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-27990/s66-27990~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":419,"size":41000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-27990/s66-27990~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1257,"size":301000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-27990/s66-27990~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]}],"metadata":{"total_hits":5}}}